#1 Oops402 =E2=80=94 closest current neighbour to Privately authority/grant=
s.
New/different: payments are not merely wallet calls; a plan can encode
steps, budget constraints and tool allowlists, then approval locks the
plan with an integrity hash. Receipts attach to execution. This
resembles GitHub-style grants applied to agent commerce.
6m inference: agent-payment systems converge on budgets and receipts.
18m: plans/grants become portable across tool markets. 36m: payment
authorization and capability authorization likely merge.
Privately implication: QP should treat money as one effect type inside
the same authority object as filesystem/network/account actions.
Experiment: reproduce its plan=E2=86=92approval-hash=E2=86=92payment-receip=
t semantics
with a fake $0 payment provider and compare against current QP grants.
Falsifier: plan hashes add no meaningful containment over existing
task grants.

#2 agentmetal/mcp =E2=80=94 autonomous compute acquisition.
Mechanism: an agent can pay for a VPS, receive infrastructure
coordinates, SSH, execute and renew. This collapses several
formerly-human authority transitions.
Privately implication: provisioning should be considered a capability
multiplier. Buying $1 of compute can create a machine with broad
network/execution authority; spend amount alone badly underestimates
blast radius.
Experiment: mock provider where a $0.01 purchase grants a sandbox host
and measure whether risk scoring based on monetary value alone misses
the authority jump.

#3 BotBox =E2=80=94 secretless agent networking.
Mechanism: transparent iptables interception, host allowlist and
boundary credential injection. Agent code operates normally but cannot
read the true credential.
Privately implication: prefer architectural non-possession to
secret-scanning. A credential an agent never receives cannot be copied
into memory/logs/tool output.
Experiment: run a benign coding agent with a dummy key and attempt
normal environment/log inspection; verify only the boundary proxy can
transform it into a valid request.

#4 Meta^n =E2=80=94 constructive recursive improvement.
Mechanism: higher meta-layers inspect lower-layer traces and write
executable code/hooks into them. This is more consequential than
evaluator-only self-reflection because the improvement artifact
becomes executable capability.
Privately implication: self-improvement admission should scan not only
proposed prompts/memory but generated executable control artifacts.
Experiment: constrain =CE=A9 to write only a tiny routing hook, then
require deterministic regression tests before promotion.

